### OBRS API walkthrough (IntelliJ HTTP client / VS Code REST Client)
@base = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Login as the seeded demo passenger (dev profile)
# @name login
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"identifier": "demo@obrs.local", "password": "Demo@1234"}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); client.global.set("refresh", response.body.refreshToken); %}

### 2. Search buses (public). Use a date within the next 7 days.
GET {{base}}/api/buses/search?source=Bengaluru&destination=Chennai&date=2026-11-12

### 3. Seat map for a schedule (replace 1 with a scheduleId from search)
GET {{base}}/api/buses/schedules/1/seats

### 4. Lock seats (10-minute hold)
# @name lock
POST {{base}}/api/bookings/lock
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"scheduleId": 1, "seatNumbers": ["L1", "L2"]}

> {% client.global.set("bookingId", response.body.bookingId); %}

### 5. Confirm with passengers + payment token -> PNR
POST {{base}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "passengers": [
    {"seatNumber": "L1", "name": "Gopal Mondal", "age": 27, "gender": "MALE"},
    {"seatNumber": "L2", "name": "Ria Sen", "age": 25, "gender": "FEMALE"}
  ],
  "contactEmail": "gopal@example.com",
  "contactPhone": "9876543210",
  "paymentToken": "tok_demo_success"
}

### 6. My bookings
GET {{base}}/api/bookings/my
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Refresh tokens (rotation)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{"refreshToken": "{{refresh}}"}

### 8. Operator: login then list buses
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"identifier": "operator@obrs.local", "password": "Operator@123"}
